::MCR_U04_L02_GP_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U04_L02_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.FL.1
Question:
Assets are $900 and liabilities are $250. What is net worth?
{
=A. $650#Correct. Net worth is assets minus liabilities: 900 - 250 \= 650.
~B. $1,150#This adds liabilities instead of subtracting them.
~C. $250#This is only liabilities, not net worth.
~D. $900#This is only assets and ignores liabilities.
}
::MCR_U04_L02_GP_Q02::
Question ID: MCR_U04_L02_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.FL.3
Question:
Net income is $1,200 and expenses are $950. How much money is left?
{
~A. $2,150#This adds income and expenses.
=B. $250#Correct. Subtract expenses from income: 1,200 - 950 \= 250.
~C. $950#This is the expense total, not leftover money.
~D. $1,200#This ignores expenses.
}
::MCR_U04_L02_GP_Q03::
Question ID: MCR_U04_L02_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.FL.1
Question:
Which item is a liability?
{
~A. cash in savings#Savings is an asset.
~B. a paid-off bicycle#An owned item with value is an asset.
=C. money owed on a loan#Correct. A liability is debt or money owed.
~D. monthly income#Income is money received, not a liability.
}
::MCR_U04_L02_GP_Q04::
Question ID: MCR_U04_L02_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.FL.3
Question:
A budget has expenses greater than income. What is the best interpretation?
{
~A. the budget has extra money#Extra money would mean income is greater than expenses.
~B. net worth is zero#Budget balance does not automatically determine net worth.
~C. assets are greater than liabilities#Assets and liabilities are not given.
=D. the budget is not balanced and needs adjustment#Correct. Expenses above income mean the plan does not fit the income constraint.
}
::MCR_U04_L02_GP_Q05::
Question ID: MCR_U04_L02_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.FL.1
Question:
Net worth is found by using which calculation?
{
~A. income minus taxes#That helps find take-home pay, not net worth.
=B. assets minus liabilities#Correct. Net worth measures what is owned minus what is owed.
~C. expenses plus income#Adding expenses and income does not find net worth.
~D. liabilities minus assets#This reverses the net worth calculation.
}
